💥The U.S. Navy just awarded Raytheon a $22.9 billion contract to accelerate Tomahawk missile production — the largest munitions deal in recent memory — as the Pentagon races to expand weapons stockpiles amid the ongoing Iran conflict.

The announcement came after Trump pushed back on concerns about strain on U.S. weapons reserves. "What we've used is peanuts," he told Fox News' Trey Yingst. "We have a lot of mid-level weapons."

The deal is designed to give RTX the stability to expand its workforce, ramp up manufacturing output, and speed deliveries of the long-range cruise missile to U.S. forces. Acting Navy Secretary Hung Cao called it a "landmark investment" that will "accelerate Tomahawk missile delivery to our warfighters at unprecedented speed."
